Add FreeType2-backed hires TrueType text rendering for Rose Tattoo UI text.

When Rose Tattoo is running in true-color hires mode, this patch lets the
engine load a vector font from
$SCUMMVM_SHERLOCK_TATTOO_ASSET_OVERRIDES/fonts/hires_font.ttf and render
crisp anti-aliased replacement text into a persistent hires overlay instead
of relying solely on nearest-neighbor-upscaled bitmap glyphs. The font is
loaded lazily, cached per pixel size in Screen::_roseTattooHiresFonts, and
queued from Fonts::writeString() once per string, with palette colors
resolved to real RGB before the hires pass.

The supporting plumbing is intentionally screen-space rather than widget-
local: BaseSurface gains setHiresTextOrigin()/clearHiresTextOrigin() so
small off-screen widget surfaces can tell Fonts::writeString() where their
text will really land, WidgetTalk sets that origin before building its
surface, WidgetBase::erase() clears the corresponding hires-text rectangle,
and Screen tracks a hires text layer plus dirty rect so update() can repaint
the smooth hires background underneath and alpha-blend the TTF glyphs on
top. The later rosetattoo-hires-tooltip-text-fix.patch is a follow-up that
builds on this core plumbing and supersedes the old widget_tooltip-specific
hunks that were accidentally captured in the corrupted dump.

